<title>FRANCE: RENAULT UNIONS CALL FOR WORK STOPPAGES FRIDAY.</title>
<headline>RENAULT UNIONS CALL FOR WORK STOPPAGES FRIDAY.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unions representing Renault workers in France, Spain and Belgium called for work stoppages on Friday to protest against the carmaker's cost-cutting measures.</p>
<p>The CFDT, CFTC and CGT unions, which represent the majority of Renault workers, said in a statement they were protesting against the planned closure of the Vilvoorde plant in Belgium, job cuts proposed in France and a reorganisation of the dealer network.</p>
<p>They will hold news conferences in Paris, Brussels and Madrid at 1300 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
